---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FeesLab from "../../components/FeesLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Real Cost of Fees"
  description="A fund fee of a fraction of a percent sounds trivial — but over a lifetime of saving it compounds into a startling share of your wealth. See the drag, and the real history of what investors actually pay."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>The real cost of fees</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A fund's fee — its <em>expense ratio</em> — is charged as a small percent of
      your balance every year, whether the fund wins or loses. One percent sounds
      like nothing. But it's skimmed off your whole balance, year after year, so it
      compounds right alongside your returns — just in the wrong direction. Move the
      sliders and watch how much a seemingly tiny fee quietly drains over a lifetime.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <FeesLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why a small fee is a big deal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Fees compound too.</strong> A 1% fee isn't 1% of your gains — it's
          1% of your <em>entire balance</em>, taken every single year. Over decades
          that can quietly consume a quarter or more of the wealth you'd otherwise
          keep, because every dollar the fee removes is a dollar that stops
          compounding for you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It's guaranteed; the outperformance isn't.</strong> You pay the
          fee whether or not the fund beats the market. Decades of evidence show
          most active funds don't beat a simple index over the long run — yet they
          charge many times more. The fee is the one part of the deal that's certain.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cost is the rare thing you control.</strong> You can't control
          markets, but you can choose a low-cost fund. That's why the real fund-fee
          history matters: the average active US equity fund charged 1.08% in 1996
          and 0.64% in 2025, while the average index equity fund charges about 0.05%.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Fees are compensation for a service, and there's nothing wrong with paying
        for genuine value. The point is to <em>see</em> the cost clearly and weigh it
        against what you're getting. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="fees" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/fees" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ss-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
